{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_sN0SQGmCnbAXrtzDI2IbqChj","content":"Title: FORERUNNER 255 SERIES Owner's Manual\nSite: Garmin\nURL: https://static.garmin.com/pumac/forerunner255series_OM_EN-SG.pdf\nSnippet: Setting Your Heart Rate Zones The watch uses your user profile information from the initial setup to determine your default heart rate zones.You can set separate heart rate zones for sport profiles,such as running, cycling, and swimming. For the most accurate calorie data during your activity, set your maximum heart rate. You can also set each heart rate zone and enter your resting heart rate manually. You can manually adjust your zones on the watch or using your Garmin Connect account. 1 Hold U\n\n---\n\nTitle: HR zone constantly changing from custom BPM to %LTHR or %HRR\nSite: Garmin Forums\nDate: 2023-11-25\nURL: https://forums.garmin.com/sports-fitness/running-multisport/f/forerunner-965/352702/hr-zone-constantly-changing-from-custom-bpm-to-lthr-or-hrr\nSnippet: Hello folks, I'm struggling with an issue that seems to be widespread and with no actual fix (found posts here, for other watch series, reddit etc.). I want my watch to use custom BPM ranges for zones, however after a random amount of time (typically a few hours) the watch switches back to %LTHR or %HRR. The issue is really frustrating because sometimes this is happening while running and as a result training effect, recovery hour and any other metrics is totally screwed. I've tried several thin\n\n---\n\nTitle: intervals-mcp by ale7canna\nSite: glama.ai\nDate: 2026-08-20\nURL: https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/ale7canna/intervals-mcp\nSnippet: Come arrivano gli allenamenti sul Garmin 1. `create_workout` scrive un evento `category: \"WORKOUT\"` sul calendario; il campo `description` contiene l'allenamento nella sintassi testuale di intervals.icu. 2. intervals.icu lo interpreta e ne costruisce la struttura ( `workout_doc`). 3. Se su intervals.icu → Settings, nel box Garmin, è attivo Upload planned workouts (con Garmin Connect autorizzato), i prossimi giorni di calendario vengono caricati su Garmin Connect e da lì arrivano all'orologio. 4.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Exact HR corridors on Garmin from Intervals.icu API workouts - Worklore\nSite: Worklore\nDate: 2026-05-12\nURL: https://worklore.dev/s/2026-05-12-exact-hr-corridors-on-garmin-from-intervals-icu-api-workouts\nSnippet: Verified end-to-end: Intervals LTHR 172, watch LTHR 168, a 75–82% target rendered 129–141 bpm on the watch — matching Intervals, drift-immune.\n\n---\n\nTitle: Custom Heart Rate range planned workout - Training\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-07-23\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/custom-heart-rate-range-planned-workout/72460\nSnippet: You need to specify the HR range in % of threshold HR. This is so workouts are portable between athletes. So if threshold HR is 170 bpm then use ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Heart rate zones compared to Garmin\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-01-17\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/heart-rate-zones-compared-to-garmin/120060\nSnippet: Garmin allows setting HR zones from LTHR and HRmax, Intervals by default only from LTHR. But there are 'custom zones' now, so you can set ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect - Page 8 - Announcements\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-08-18\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521?page=8\nSnippet: I think Garmin inserts absolute BPM values while Intervals expects %LTHR. It may sound strange but you are probably one of the few users using ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Intervals.icu and Garmin sync for right intensities - Training\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2024-02-05\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/intervals-icu-and-garmin-sync-for-right-intensities/59698\nSnippet: In Intervals you are using Heart Rate (LTHR). These won't give the same result as they are different units of measure. If I understand, your ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: Workout Builder Syntax Quick Guide\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2026-03-03\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-syntax-quick-guide/123701\nSnippet: Heart rate. Percent of max HR: 70% HR , 75-80% HR; Percent of threshold HR: 95% LTHR , 90-95% LTHR; HR zones: Z2 HR , Z2-Z3 HR. Pace. Percent of ...\n\n---\n\nTitle: \nSite: fitstore24.com\nURL: https://www.fitstore24.com/media/files/263843-Bedienungsanleitung_Horizon_Elite_T5.1_Elite_T7.1.pdf\nSnippet: INTERVAL HR: Interval heart rate is the best program to improve cardio performance, you can set two different heart rate value, one is workout heart rate, the other one is rest heart rate to have the interval training. HEART RATE ZONE PROGRAM NOTE: - The chest strap is required to use the HRC program, with HRC program you can only choose time as your workout target. - Target heart rate is selected in multiples of 5 beats. - If there is no heart rate detected, the unit will not change the speed o\n\n---\n\nTitle: Garmin preset for Heart Rate Zones (%LTHR based) - Feature Requests - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2022-11-21\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/garmin-preset-for-heart-rate-zones-lthr-based/24197\nSnippet: post by ggarcea on Nov 21, 2022 Hello! I’m matching the heart rate and power zones to my Garmin 955 and I can’t seem to find a preset that matches the Garmin default zones based on %LTHR. For power, Garmin seems to match perfectly the Friel preset for cycling and the MyProCoach Run for running. Would it be possible to add it (it seems to be the same for cycling, running and generic sport zones)? Or am I missing a preset that matches? These are the default Garmin Zones: Garmin LTHR Zones Thanks! \n\n---\n\nTitle: Heart rate zones and LTHR issues - Bug Reports - Intervals.icu Forum\nSite: Intervals.icu Forum\nDate: 2020-05-06\nURL: https://forum.intervals.icu/t/heart-rate-zones-and-lthr-issues/854\nSnippet: When viewing the HR chart, however, I can see that my MaxHR for the effort was actually 196. I would expect that after updating the MaxHR in the settings and selecting to “apply to all previous rides”, this would correct the Max HR shown at the top of the activity screen. Screenshots attached for clarity. Screen Shot 2020-05-07 at 12.52.35 AM If you max hr for a ride was recorded as 195, then that either is your max hr (and not 187) or a spike. The value is recorded at the time of the activity -\n\n---\n\nTitle: Heart Rate Zone Methods Compared: MaxHR% vs HRR vs LTHR\nSite: Hashiri.AI\nURL: https://hashiri.ai/knowledge/heart-rate-zone-methods\nSnippet: Method 3: Lactate Threshold Heart Rate (LTHR) LTHR-based zones are anchored to your actual lactate threshold — the intensity where lactate starts accumulating faster than your body can clear it. This is the most physiologically meaningful reference point because it directly reflects your current metabolic fitness. Rather than using generic percentages of MaxHR, LTHR zones define each zone relative to your threshold heart rate. Zone 2 sits well below threshold, Zone 4 brackets it, and Zone 5 is a\n\nWhen you rely on a result in your answer, cite it inline as a markdown link, e.g. [title](url)."}
